# Header rules for Cloudflare Pages / Netlify — the mirror of vercel.json's
# `headers`. Ignored by Vercel, which stays the production host.
#
# The service worker must never be cached, or an installed PWA can pin itself to
# a stale build and stop picking up deploys. (The manifest's
# application/manifest+json Content-Type is already the default on both hosts,
# so unlike vercel.json there is no rule for it here — neither host lets
# _headers override Content-Type anyway.)
/sw.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
